(c) Keyboard + ARIA
- `aria-current="page"` probed on /dashboard and /accounts (2 different
  pages): each time exactly the correct link (desktop copy AND mobile copy)
  carries aria-current, no false positive on the other tab.
- Mobile toggle: before open aria-expanded=false, aria-controls="mobile-nav";
  focused #mobile-nav-toggle and pressed Enter (real keyboard, no click()):
  aria-expanded flips to true, #mobile-nav loses .hidden. aria-controls
  resolves to the real panel id.
- Tab-walk from the open mobile menu visits all 8 links in visual/group
  order (dashboard, explorer, insights, major-expenses, whatif, accounts,
  transfers, filemanager) then continues into page content — no trap, no
  skipped/duplicated stop.
- Group labels: role="group" + aria-labelledby resolves to a real, VISIBLE
  text node in both desktop (span, text-white/60, labelVisible:true) and
  mobile (p, same, labelVisible:true) — confirmed via getComputedStyle +
  offsetParent, not just DOM presence.
- Heading order: 0 headings inside <nav> (group labels are span/p, not
  h2/h3, avoiding a heading-hierarchy complaint); /dashboard heading
  sequence is H1,H2,H2,H2,H2,H2,H2 — no skip, no heading was inserted
  before the page's own H1.
- No `outline-none`/`outline:none` anywhere in the nav markup — default
  focus ring survives on every link and the toggle button.

